msgid "Vert.x Reference Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://vertx.io[Vert.x] is a toolkit for building reactive applications.\n"
"As described in the xref:quarkus-reactive-architecture.adoc[Quarkus Reactive "
"Architecture], Quarkus uses Vert.x underneath."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This guide is the companion to the xref:vertx.adoc[Using Eclipse Vert.x API "
"from a Quarkus Application] guide.\n"
"It provides more advanced details about the usage and the configuration of "
"the Vert.x instance used by Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accessing the Vert.x instance"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To access the managed Vert.x instance, add the `quarkus-vertx` extension to "
"your project.\n"
"Note that this dependency may already be installed (as a transitive "
"dependency)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With this extension, you can retrieve the managed instance of Vert.x using "
"either field or constructor injection:"
msgstr ""

msgid "You can inject either the:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`io.vertx.core.Vertx` instance exposing the _bare_ Vert.x API"
msgstr ""

msgid "`io.vertx.mutiny.core.Vertx` instance exposing the _Mutiny_ API"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We recommend using the Mutiny variant as it integrates with the other "
"reactive APIs provided by Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mutiny"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are not familiar with Mutiny, check xref:mutiny-primer.adoc[Mutiny - "
"an intuitive reactive programming library]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Documentation about the Vert.x Mutiny variant is available on https://"
"smallrye.io/smallrye-mutiny-vertx-bindings."
msgstr ""

